# `npm version` tags releases as `<tag-version-prefix><version>` (e.g. `v1.0.0`
# by default). This repo has real, pushed tags `v0.1.1` through `v5.0.0` left
# over from before the @pmealha/eidos-ui → eidos-ui rename/version reset - git
# tags have no awareness of the package rename, so any new release that
# reaches a version number matching one of those old tags collides with it
# (hit this exactly at 1.0.0 - see CHANGELOG.md's "Fresh start" entry for the
# rename itself). A distinct prefix avoids this permanently without needing to
# delete any of that real historical history.
tag-version-prefix=eidos-v
